	Trial_10: Shadow That Mimics a Walk
	Trial_11: Flower Opened Wrong
	Trial_12: Guard in the Stone House
	Trial_13: Those at the Door
	Trial_14: Far Side of the Moon
	Trial_15: Fire in the Earth's Heart
	Trial_16: Ghosts in a Clump
	Trial_17: God-Eater
	Trial_18: Dragon Still Alive
	Trial_19: The Maker's Iron
	Trial_20: That Witch
	Trial_21: Night Gathering Again
	TrialSummary_0: There's something hanging in the sky that won't blink. Looking at it makes me tired. Go make it close its eyes.
	TrialSummary_1: In the dirt it's either a worm or a brain. Whichever's filthier, cut that. The blade will know the taste.
	TrialSummary_2: The filth has bunched up. The source is there—help me cut it loose.
	TrialSummary_3: A puddle of sugar calling itself a god. If names were that easy, I'd be a goddess already. Go take its name off.
	TrialSummary_4: The road's blocked by a wall of meat. Cut straight through. What's past it sits heavier than here.
	TrialSummary_5: A worm surfaced on the brimstone sea. One open mouth and it reeks. Don't let it near the shore.
	TrialSummary_6: Something in the lava is still burning. When the flame goes out, that place can breathe again.
	TrialSummary_7: An iron long-worm. The first one. Cut it open—don't race it for length.
	TrialSummary_8: Two eyes in the sky, pretending to be a pair of people. One at a time.
	TrialSummary_9: An iron lump wearing an old king's skull. Take the head and the rest is just parts.
	TrialSummary_10: A shadow copying someone else's walk. The closer it gets, the more it bothers me. Help me cut it down.
	TrialSummary_11: A flower opened underground that shouldn't have. When it falls, the ground air clears a little.
	TrialSummary_12: A guard in a stone house that won't blink. Wake it up—or put it to sleep.
	TrialSummary_13: People muttering at the dungeon door. The rite isn't finished—interrupt them.
	TrialSummary_14: Something's pressed against the far side of the moon. Peel it open. The world gets lighter.
	TrialSummary_15: A fire that won't go cold lives in the earth's heart. Go see it. The blade will run hot—bear with it.
	TrialSummary_16: Ghosts stuck in one clump. Don't count them. Split the whole mass and they scatter.
	TrialSummary_17: It has eaten gods. We aren't gods—but if a blade fears gods, it's only iron. Go.
	TrialSummary_18: One dragon left in the world. Go see it. If a feather falls, pick one up for me too.
	TrialSummary_19: Someone built themselves an iron giant. The core's inside—pull it out and it stops.
	TrialSummary_20: That witch. Where she stays, the night turns sticky. Go end her.
	TrialSummary_21: They're gathering again. Like a night that won't break. The longest cut is yours. I'll watch.
}
